cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, its benchmark, or its evidence chain, please cite it as below."
title: "SQCAD: Scope-Qualified Competitive Access Decay for evidence-governed Agent Memory"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Topps-2025/SQCAD"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research prototype for governing the future access of Agent Memory under a
  fixed workspace budget. SQCAD separates evidence records, scope-qualified
  permission (point/bound/unresolved/mismatch) and competitive access
  projection, with reversible archive and paid restore/probe channels. The
  framework is reverse-derived from formal results on memory-specific
  identification gaps, self-obscuring lifecycle dynamics and minimax probing
  lower bounds.
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - memory governance
  - causal identification
  - lifecycle value
  - selective forgetting
  - memory benchmarks
  - lifecyclebench
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-02
